                  "snaktype": "value",
                  "property": "P1683",
                  "hash": "ebecb7fe06484d287a8a976768b78f77de96cb68",
                  "datavalue": {
                    "value": {
                      "text": "The Hi{{okina}}iaka density of {{val|0.685|0.134|ul=g/cm3}} reported by Vara Lubiano in 2023 uses the outdated Hi{{okina}}iaka mass of {{val|1.8|0.1|e=19|ul=kg}} from 2009. Proudfoot et al. (2024) measured a lower mass for Hi{{okina}}iaka, which means the density of Hi{{okina}}iaka is must also be lower, if one uses Vara Lubiano's diameter measurement. Dividing the Proudfoot et al.'s (2024) mass by the volume calculated from Vara Lubiano's mean sphere-equivalent diameter gives a density of {{cvt|461 ± 149|kg/m3|g/cm3}} (uncertainties calculated via [[propagation of error]]).",
                      "language": "en"
                    },
                    "type": "monolingualtext"
                  },
                  "datatype": "monolingualtext"
                }
              ]
            },
            "snaks-order": [
